=== ''Baizuka'' ===
{| class="wikitable" |- |Sakakiyama Kofun (Tsukuriyama No. 1) |{{nihongo|''{{ill|Round Kofun|lt=empun|ja|円墳|1=Round Kofun|1=Round Kofun|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Round Kofun|13=User:Immanuelle/Round Kofun|comment=enwiki is a redirect}}''|円墳|1=Round Kofun|1=Round Kofun}} circuler mound or {{nihongo|''[[Zenpō-kōen-fun|zenpō-kōen-fun]]''|前方後円墳|lt=Zenpō-kōen-fun|1=Zenpō-kōen-fun|comment=doing this because I need to differentiate it in piped links too with my new interwiki tool as not the ambiguous phrase keyhole shaped kofun|1=Zenpō-kōen-fun|1=[[Zenpō-kōen-fun]]|2=前方後円墳|3=|4=}} |Rear circle diameter about 40m |A horse-shaped belt hook was excavated. In addition, a divine beast mirror and copper bells were excavated. |- |Tsukuriyama No. 2 |{{nihongo|''{{ill|Square Kofun|lt=hōfun|ja|方墳|1=Square Kofun|1=Square Kofun|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Square Kofun|13=User:Immanuelle/Square Kofun|comment=enwiki is a redirect}}''|方墳|1=Square Kofun|1=Square Kofun}} square mound |About 40 meters on a side | Surrounding moat exists. More than 100 ''haniwa'' were unearthed in a row on the outer bank. |- |Tsukuriyama No. 3 |{{nihongo|''{{ill|Round Kofun|lt=empun|ja|円墳|1=Round Kofun|1=Round Kofun|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Round Kofun|13=User:Immanuelle/Round Kofun|comment=enwiki is a redirect}}''|円墳|1=Round Kofun|1=Round Kofun}} (uncertain) |Diameter about 30 meters | |- |Tsukuriyama No. 4 |{{nihongo|''{{ill|Round Kofun|lt=empun|ja|円墳|1=Round Kofun|1=Round Kofun|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Round Kofun|13=User:Immanuelle/Round Kofun|comment=enwiki is a redirect}}''|円墳|1=Round Kofun|1=Round Kofun}} circular mound or {{nihongo|''[[Zenpō-kōen-fun|zenpō-kōen-fun]]''|前方後円墳|lt=Zenpō-kōen-fun|1=Zenpō-kōen-fun|comment=doing this because I need to differentiate it in piped links too with my new interwiki tool as not the ambiguous phrase keyhole shaped kofun|1=Zenpō-kōen-fun|1=[[Zenpō-kōen-fun]]|2=前方後円墳|3=|4=}} |Length 55 meters |Cylindrical and figurative ''haniwa'' (house-shaped and armor-shaped) excavated from the edge of the mound. |- |Senzoku Kofun (Tsukuriyama No. 5) |{{nihongo|{{ill|scallop-shaped kofun|lt=''hotategata'' kofun|ja|帆立貝形古墳|1=scallop-shaped kofun|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/scallop-shaped kofun|13=User:Immanuelle/scallop-shaped kofun|comment=enwiki is a redirect}}|帆立貝形古墳||}} scallop-shaped kofun |Length 75 meters |Construction of 3 stages. It has an early horizontal stone chamber similar to the ornamental Kofuns in the northwestern part of Kyushu. In the stone chamber, there is a stone partition carved with a straight arc pattern. |- |Tsukuriyama No. 6 |{{nihongo|''{{ill|Round Kofun|lt=empun|ja|円墳|1=Round Kofun|1=Round Kofun|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Round Kofun|13=User:Immanuelle/Round Kofun|comment=enwiki is a redirect}}''|円墳|1=Round Kofun|1=Round Kofun}} circular mound |Diameter 30 meters |It has a horizontal stone chamber. |- |}
